1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,232
[This drama is a work of fiction]

2
00:00:07,232 --> 00:00:08,633
[All scenes involving animals and children
were filmed in compliance with regulations]

3
00:00:49,112 --> 00:00:52,052
You punk, serves you right!
You piece of crap...

4
00:00:52,052 --> 00:00:54,649
You piece of crap, you punk!

5
00:01:15,144 --> 00:01:19,448
[Episode 4, 99 Million Won]

6
00:01:19,448 --> 00:01:21,720
Bad luck, go away.

7
00:01:21,720 --> 00:01:23,748
Go away!

8
00:01:23,748 --> 00:01:25,083
Let everything go our way.

9
00:01:26,072 --> 00:01:28,224
Let everything go our way.

10
00:01:28,224 --> 00:01:30,124
Let's pay off the loan

11
00:01:31,540 --> 00:01:33,488
and just get the investment.

12
00:01:33,488 --> 00:01:35,600
Please, just let the investment come through.

13
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:38,028
We'll change the car too.

14
00:01:38,028 --> 00:01:39,816
We need to replace the car first.

15
00:01:39,816 --> 00:01:42,512
- Ugh, this gives me the creeps.
- Honey! Honey!

16
00:01:42,512 --> 00:01:44,949
What's this? Look at this, look!

17
00:01:45,888 --> 00:01:47,684
"I recorded

18
00:01:47,684 --> 00:01:50,020
everything you did yesterday.

19
00:01:50,020 --> 00:01:53,128
Cash, 500 million won,

20
00:01:53,128 --> 00:01:55,068
today at 5?"

21
00:01:55,068 --> 00:01:56,404
Is this person insane?

22
00:01:56,404 --> 00:01:57,892
It says they'll release the video

23
00:01:57,892 --> 00:02:00,383
if we're even one second late after 5.
What do we do?

24
00:02:02,183 --> 00:02:03,216
[Would you like to open the link?]

25
00:02:03,216 --> 00:02:04,516
What video? Huh?

26
00:02:04,516 --> 00:02:05,704
[Breaking! The shocking secret
of a perfect family]

27
00:02:05,704 --> 00:02:07,848
What did they record?

28
00:02:07,848 --> 00:02:09,376
What on earth is this?

29
00:02:09,376 --> 00:02:11,604
Exactly.

30
00:02:11,604 --> 00:02:13,836
- But how did they even get my number?
- Yesterday?

31
00:02:13,836 --> 00:02:16,084
What about yesterday? Yesterday, we...

32
00:02:16,084 --> 00:02:18,760
- Does this person know us?
- What video? Huh?

33
00:02:18,760 --> 00:02:20,960
- This is driving me crazy, seriously...
- Hey!

34
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:23,464
Are you sure they actually recorded a video?

35
00:02:23,464 --> 00:02:25,949
There was nobody there yesterday.

36
00:02:26,940 --> 00:02:29,280
Isn't this a bluff?

37
00:02:29,280 --> 00:02:31,149
How would I know?

38
00:02:35,824 --> 00:02:39,416
I don't know what kind of video you have,

39
00:02:40,648 --> 00:02:44,816
but you can't threaten innocent people.

40
00:02:45,916 --> 00:02:47,772
[I don't know what kind of video you have,
but you can't threaten innocent people]

41
00:02:47,772 --> 00:02:48,808
Darn it.

42
00:02:48,808 --> 00:02:50,316
- There's no way this is going through...
- Darn it, darn it, darn it!

43
00:02:50,316 --> 00:02:52,820
Darn it, darn it, darn it, darn it, darn it!

44
00:02:52,820 --> 00:02:55,268
That's why I told you
we should've turned her in yesterday!

45
00:02:55,268 --> 00:02:58,872
Why did you move the body without a plan?

46
00:02:58,872 --> 00:03:01,720
You said we'd do it together!

47
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:05,272
You took all the stuff out of the car,
and crammed that body...

48
00:03:05,272 --> 00:03:08,864
that man in, who didn't even
fit in the car, huh?

49
00:03:08,864 --> 00:03:11,224
Who was the one pouring paint on the ground,

50
00:03:11,224 --> 00:03:13,318
pushing it around, wiping it, sweeping it?

51
00:03:13,318 --> 00:03:16,956
I thought you were filming some
YouTube video in a demolition area!

52
00:03:16,956 --> 00:03:19,188
Is this really the time to argue
whose fault it is?

53
00:03:19,188 --> 00:03:22,484
We don't even know
if we'll make it out alive,

54
00:03:22,484 --> 00:03:25,583
so what are we going to do
about this message?

55
00:03:25,583 --> 00:03:27,950
Why are you yelling at me?

56
00:03:27,950 --> 00:03:31,112
Why would we hand over
that much money to that punk?

57
00:03:31,112 --> 00:03:34,032
If we give them the money
and they still upload the video,

58
00:03:34,032 --> 00:03:37,183
we're screwed twice over!

59
00:03:37,183 --> 00:03:39,940
It says we have until 5 p.m. today.

60
00:03:39,940 --> 00:03:41,916
Do you have another idea?

61
00:03:50,804 --> 00:03:52,976
I mean,

62
00:03:52,976 --> 00:03:54,436
how are we supposed to

63
00:03:54,436 --> 00:03:57,049
get 500 million won in cash in half a day?

64
00:03:58,520 --> 00:04:03,949
We have some cash in the safe,
so let's start with that first.

65
00:04:05,676 --> 00:04:10,016
Honey, how much cash
did we have left in the safe?

66
00:04:10,016 --> 00:04:12,048
- Wasn't it a few hundred million won?
- A few hundred million won?

67
00:04:12,048 --> 00:04:13,812
Didn't we have gold bars and everything?

68
00:04:13,812 --> 00:04:15,252
- Yeah, there's a few hundred million won.
- Yeah.

69
00:04:15,252 --> 00:04:17,183
Oh, Ye Ji, you're up?

70
00:04:24,458 --> 00:04:27,383
Hong, I've been thinking.

71
00:04:27,383 --> 00:04:29,604
I think I can handle it.

72
00:04:29,604 --> 00:04:31,684
[VAULT1932, Feel free to leave an inquiry]
So honey, don't worry too much.

73
00:04:31,684 --> 00:04:33,640
[Customer information is kept private]
Ah, what is this?

74
00:04:33,640 --> 00:04:37,409
Why do I need to make a reservation
to use my own safe?

75
00:04:37,409 --> 00:04:40,012
I'll go to the safe alone later.

76
00:04:40,012 --> 00:04:42,716
Honey, didn't you say you were
meeting the Townhouse writer today?

77
00:04:42,716 --> 00:04:44,883
Oh, that's next week.

78
00:04:46,012 --> 00:04:48,424
- Well, that left one is pretty.
- Yeah.

79
00:04:48,424 --> 00:04:52,436
Honey, you were supposed
to meet Michelle today.

80
00:04:52,436 --> 00:04:55,468
And the safe reservation is under my name,

81
00:04:55,468 --> 00:04:57,083
so I have to go myself.

82
00:05:00,236 --> 00:05:01,783
Hong!

83
00:05:03,352 --> 00:05:05,920
There's no cash in the safe.

84
00:05:05,920 --> 00:05:07,448
I'm sorry.

85
00:05:07,448 --> 00:05:09,012
What?

86
00:05:09,012 --> 00:05:13,008
Oh, come on... you know.

87
00:05:13,008 --> 00:05:15,680
Michelle said she'd invest,
but then suddenly backed out.

88
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:17,564
I already told all our clients.

89
00:05:17,564 --> 00:05:19,949
The factory already received all the orders.

90
00:05:22,428 --> 00:05:24,852
But we did receive
the final payment last week.

91
00:05:24,852 --> 00:05:27,568
That and the company funds, no,

92
00:05:27,568 --> 00:05:30,284
with the gold bars in the safe,

93
00:05:30,284 --> 00:05:32,916
it might have been enough.

94
00:05:32,916 --> 00:05:36,452
Wait, you made all those decisions
without even discussing them with me!

95
00:05:36,452 --> 00:05:38,083
Aren't we married?

96
00:05:41,034 --> 00:05:43,208
Seriously, just because you're
a little more successful than me

97
00:05:43,208 --> 00:05:46,008
and appear on TV a little more,

98
00:05:46,008 --> 00:05:48,552
there's a limit to how much
you can disrespect your husband!

99
00:05:48,552 --> 00:05:51,849
How can you always
make decisions on your own?

100
00:05:53,264 --> 00:05:55,176
I'm sorry.

101
00:05:55,176 --> 00:05:58,016
I'm really sorry. It's all my fault.

102
00:06:00,724 --> 00:06:03,872
What are we going to do now? Huh?

103
00:06:03,872 --> 00:06:07,636
Where are we supposed to
get that much money all of a sudden?

104
00:06:07,636 --> 00:06:10,536
If the video gets leaked suddenly like this,

105
00:06:10,536 --> 00:06:12,016
then my life...

106
00:06:13,972 --> 00:06:17,383
Then what about Ye Ji's future?

107
00:06:18,608 --> 00:06:21,083
I'll figure something out. Okay?

108
00:06:22,316 --> 00:06:24,149
I'll fix everything, honey.

109
00:06:25,516 --> 00:06:26,949
Okay?

110
00:06:31,848 --> 00:06:36,649
If anyone asks about the wound,
say you hit yourself under the bed.

111
00:06:37,948 --> 00:06:39,449
Okay.

112
00:06:44,696 --> 00:06:46,416
Act like nothing happened.

113
00:06:48,732 --> 00:06:50,968
- Oh, hello.
- Hello.

114
00:06:50,968 --> 00:06:52,264
Hello!

115
00:06:52,264 --> 00:06:54,292
Oh my, Min Seo, you got bangs!

116
00:06:54,292 --> 00:06:56,636
They suit you perfectly. Right, Ye Ji?

117
00:06:56,636 --> 00:07:00,364
Oh, yes, I think they're pretty too,
but Min Seo doesn't seem to like them at all.

118
00:07:00,364 --> 00:07:02,032
We'll be late. Shall we go, Ye Ji?

119
00:07:02,032 --> 00:07:03,583
- Yeah.
- Ye Ji, have a good day.

120
00:07:07,564 --> 00:07:09,788
She didn't notice, right?

121
00:07:09,788 --> 00:07:11,980
Notice what?

122
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:14,983
You're a pro at hiding things.

123
00:07:30,316 --> 00:07:36,520
[Cheongnam Police Station]

124
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:38,649
Honey, you know I trust you, right?

125
00:07:48,216 --> 00:07:50,249
No, but look where I got hit! Look at it!

126
00:07:50,249 --> 00:07:52,320
Yeah, that hit, it looks red
because you're drunk.

127
00:07:52,320 --> 00:07:53,483
- Please sit down for a moment.
- You!

128
00:07:53,483 --> 00:07:55,249
- What are you talking about?
- Sir, lower your voice.

129
00:07:55,249 --> 00:07:56,752
Sir!

130
00:07:56,752 --> 00:07:58,736
You shouldn't be shouting like that.

131
00:07:58,736 --> 00:08:02,024
Just sit down and talk. We'll listen calmly.

132
00:08:02,024 --> 00:08:03,049
You have to hear me out!

133
00:08:03,049 --> 00:08:05,516
We're listening to you!
So sit down and talk to us!

134
00:08:05,516 --> 00:08:07,460
Why are you acting like this?

135
00:08:07,460 --> 00:08:09,268
You're drunk in the middle of the day.

136
00:08:09,268 --> 00:08:12,049
Please wait. We'll take care of it.

137
00:08:12,960 --> 00:08:15,510
Yeah, how can I help you?

138
00:08:15,510 --> 00:08:16,584
Yeah, well...

139
00:08:16,584 --> 00:08:18,716
Hello.

140
00:08:19,617 --> 00:08:23,912
I lost my car last night.

141
00:08:23,912 --> 00:08:25,364
Well...

142
00:08:25,364 --> 00:08:27,512
I parked my car near the stream
by my vacation house

143
00:08:27,512 --> 00:08:29,676
in Yongsin-dong to go for a jog...

144
00:08:29,676 --> 00:08:31,372
Huh?

145
00:08:31,372 --> 00:08:34,832
Are you Model House's...

146
00:08:34,832 --> 00:08:37,116
Cha...

147
00:08:37,116 --> 00:08:39,220
Cha Eun Bin.

148
00:08:39,220 --> 00:08:40,984
- Yeah.
- Wow!

149
00:08:40,984 --> 00:08:43,172
Townhouse, not Model House.

150
00:08:43,172 --> 00:08:45,296
Oh, yes.

151
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:48,532
My mom is a huge fan of that drama.

152
00:08:48,532 --> 00:08:49,808
- Oh, really?
- Yeah.

153
00:08:49,808 --> 00:08:51,220
- Oh, is that so?
- Yeah.

154
00:08:51,220 --> 00:08:52,796
Then would you like me
to sign something for her?

155
00:08:52,796 --> 00:08:55,849
- Thank you. Just one, please.
- Of course.

156
00:08:56,692 --> 00:08:58,583
Here, two, please.

157
00:09:00,463 --> 00:09:02,049
Oh, hello.

158
00:09:04,085 --> 00:09:07,183
You said your car went missing
in Yongsin-dong, right?

159
00:09:08,252 --> 00:09:10,140
Yes.

160
00:09:10,140 --> 00:09:12,484
Then why didn't you go to the local precinct
right away

161
00:09:12,484 --> 00:09:14,849
but came here a day later?

162
00:09:16,464 --> 00:09:18,949
Well, it's just...

163
00:09:21,356 --> 00:09:23,528
You were flustered, I see. Oh, dear.

164
00:09:23,528 --> 00:09:27,132
Yeah, I was flustered.

165
00:09:27,132 --> 00:09:30,384
But you were taking a walk in Yongsin-dong?

166
00:09:30,384 --> 00:09:32,368
You know that neighborhood
is dangerous, right?

167
00:09:32,368 --> 00:09:33,783
Sorry?

168
00:09:34,652 --> 00:09:37,249
It has the highest crime rate around here.

169
00:09:40,628 --> 00:09:42,856
Yeah, I know.

170
00:09:42,856 --> 00:09:44,869
[Unpyeong City Yongsin-dong crime]
Look at this, see?

171
00:09:44,869 --> 00:09:47,428
"Used as a crime hotspot by organized gangs."

172
00:09:47,428 --> 00:09:50,160
- Oh, dear.
- No wonder it was so cheap.

173
00:09:50,160 --> 00:09:54,083
I told you from the start
that realtor gave me a bad feeling.

174
00:09:54,083 --> 00:09:57,116
So, did the cops say anything else?

175
00:09:59,388 --> 00:10:01,820
I gave them my best
method-acting performance,

176
00:10:01,820 --> 00:10:05,404
and they bought it immediately.

177
00:10:05,404 --> 00:10:09,856
They even worried about how much
I must've suffered all night.

178
00:10:09,856 --> 00:10:12,816
That's my husband.
I could never have pulled that off.

179
00:10:15,296 --> 00:10:17,244
Honey,

180
00:10:17,244 --> 00:10:20,249
what would you ever do without me?

181
00:10:21,296 --> 00:10:23,012
I wouldn't have survived.

182
00:10:23,012 --> 00:10:24,836
Oh, and I've been thinking.

183
00:10:24,836 --> 00:10:27,768
First, we can cover it with company funds.

184
00:10:27,768 --> 00:10:29,256
Oh, really?

185
00:10:29,256 --> 00:10:32,116
- Are you sure?
- Yeah. Well, for now.

186
00:10:34,644 --> 00:10:38,942
[5 Hours Before the Video Release]

187
00:10:38,942 --> 00:10:41,124
Why not?

188
00:10:41,124 --> 00:10:43,548
We classify those payments
as temporary advances all the time.

189
00:10:43,548 --> 00:10:45,372
You said it wasn't a big deal.

190
00:10:45,372 --> 00:10:47,188
<i>You know better than I do,</i>

191
00:10:47,188 --> 00:10:50,572
<i>but there's the risk of a tax audit,
and the investment is on the line.</i>

192
00:10:50,572 --> 00:10:54,883
<i>What if Michelle Jung makes a fuss
about it and pulls out her investment?</i>

193
00:10:55,932 --> 00:10:57,849
Why can't I withdraw it?

194
00:10:59,140 --> 00:11:02,783
Banks don't keep much cash
on hand these days.

195
00:11:02,783 --> 00:11:05,296
The maximum you can withdraw
today is 300 million won.

196
00:11:05,296 --> 00:11:07,440
Well, if you make a reservation,

197
00:11:07,440 --> 00:11:11,204
you can withdraw the rest
tomorrow or the next day.

198
00:11:11,204 --> 00:11:13,049
What would you like to do?

199
00:11:16,916 --> 00:11:19,183
[Director Kwak: Why are you suddenly
withdrawing that much money?]

200
00:11:19,183 --> 00:11:20,249
[Is something going on?
What if this hurts the company?]

201
00:11:20,249 --> 00:11:22,316
[Where are you now?
Why aren't you answering?]

202
00:11:23,648 --> 00:11:25,395
Please withdraw all 300 million won.

203
00:11:25,395 --> 00:11:27,849
Yeah, understood.

204
00:11:29,556 --> 00:11:31,249
So, what happened?

205
00:11:33,036 --> 00:11:38,656
I can't believe you withdrew
all that cash without even talking to me.

206
00:11:38,656 --> 00:11:41,604
I heard gold prices have gone up.

207
00:11:41,604 --> 00:11:44,732
If we sell all the gold bars,
how much would it be?

208
00:11:44,732 --> 00:11:47,949
Well, if we sell all this,
it'll be about 90 million won.

209
00:11:48,832 --> 00:11:51,832
But you said the company money
would cover it all. Then what's this?

210
00:11:51,832 --> 00:11:53,444
Now we're selling the gold bars too?

211
00:11:53,444 --> 00:11:55,340
I know. How was I supposed to know

212
00:11:55,340 --> 00:11:57,070
the bank would only let us
withdraw 300 million won?

213
00:11:57,070 --> 00:11:59,324
The bank doesn't have that much cash.

214
00:11:59,324 --> 00:12:02,623
I tried to withdraw more from other places,

215
00:12:02,623 --> 00:12:04,908
but Director Kwak went ballistic, saying

216
00:12:04,908 --> 00:12:08,790
we absolutely couldn't make
that many withdrawals in one day.

217
00:12:08,790 --> 00:12:12,652
So, we've got my 300 million won
and 90 million won from the gold bars.

218
00:12:12,652 --> 00:12:15,208
We just need about another 110 million won.

219
00:12:15,208 --> 00:12:17,068
Honey,

220
00:12:17,068 --> 00:12:19,740
<i>do you happen to know anywhere
we could borrow about 100 million won?</i>

221
00:12:19,740 --> 00:12:21,892
<i>I'll keep looking too,</i>

222
00:12:21,892 --> 00:12:24,649
<i>but I have a meeting
with Michelle right away.</i>

223
00:12:25,828 --> 00:12:27,616
I got it.

224
00:12:33,948 --> 00:12:37,716
Where am I supposed to get
100 million won in cash in just a few hours?

225
00:12:40,092 --> 00:12:45,049
Of course. I'm a married man too.
I totally understand, yeah.

226
00:12:49,049 --> 00:12:53,183
I'm getting a call right now.
I'll call you back later, yeah.

227
00:12:54,040 --> 00:12:55,160
- Yeah.
- <i>Yeah, it's me.</i>

228
00:12:55,160 --> 00:12:57,372
- What happened?
- <i>I managed to scrape together some money.</i>

229
00:12:57,372 --> 00:13:00,183
- Oh, really?
- <i>But it's not much.</i>

230
00:13:00,183 --> 00:13:02,900
- How much?
- <i>About a million won?</i>

231
00:13:02,900 --> 00:13:06,244
<i>- That's too little, right?</i>
- Oh... a million won?

232
00:13:06,244 --> 00:13:08,632
<i>Yeah, I've been spending everything
on raising the baby.</i>

233
00:13:08,632 --> 00:13:12,612
Well, yeah, the economy is bad these days.
A million won is a lot of money.

234
00:13:12,612 --> 00:13:13,896
Thanks so much.

235
00:13:13,896 --> 00:13:15,653
<i>Don't thank me. I'm the one who's sorry.</i>

236
00:13:15,653 --> 00:13:19,849
What do you have to be sorry for?
I'm the one asking to borrow money.

237
00:13:19,849 --> 00:13:22,616
<i>Alright, let's grab a drink sometime.</i>

238
00:13:22,616 --> 00:13:26,256
Anyway, I'll text you
my account number. Yeah.

239
00:13:26,256 --> 00:13:29,183
- Thanks.
- <i>Yeah, send it over, and I'll transfer it.</i>

240
00:13:30,649 --> 00:13:33,583
[Min Woo]

241
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:36,248
Yeah, can you?

242
00:13:36,248 --> 00:13:38,149
About 100 million won?

243
00:13:39,954 --> 00:13:41,516
Right.

244
00:13:42,258 --> 00:13:45,083
This is pretty sudden, isn't it?

245
00:13:46,036 --> 00:13:48,332
Yeah, I know. I know.

246
00:13:48,332 --> 00:13:50,133
Sorry for asking you out of the blue.

247
00:13:50,133 --> 00:13:52,883
- Oh dear!
- Oh dear, Chairwoman.

248
00:13:53,592 --> 00:13:55,849
- It's been a while.
- Yes, Chairwoman, what brings you here?

249
00:13:55,849 --> 00:13:58,549
I have a quick meeting here.

250
00:13:59,928 --> 00:14:01,740
Oh, no, no.

251
00:14:01,740 --> 00:14:03,756
- Your health's been good?
- Yeah.

252
00:14:03,756 --> 00:14:04,970
Business going well?

253
00:14:04,970 --> 00:14:07,552
Yes, thankfully.

254
00:14:07,552 --> 00:14:10,384
Yeah, I'll treat you to a meal sometime.

255
00:14:10,384 --> 00:14:12,049
Good luck with your meeting.

256
00:14:15,336 --> 00:14:16,849
Thanks.

257
00:14:23,976 --> 00:14:25,449
Captain Park?

258
00:14:26,584 --> 00:14:28,316
Right? Home Makeover.

259
00:14:29,320 --> 00:14:31,071
Wow, I'm a fan.

260
00:14:31,071 --> 00:14:32,664
Oh...

261
00:14:32,664 --> 00:14:38,016
Wow! You look even more impressive in person.

262
00:14:38,016 --> 00:14:40,616
- Thanks, and hello.
- Yeah.

263
00:14:40,616 --> 00:14:42,252
- I'm currently...
- I was actually

264
00:14:42,252 --> 00:14:44,905
looking for an interior contractor.

265
00:14:44,905 --> 00:14:47,360
Wow, can't believe I ran into you here.

266
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:48,768
- What a coincidence.
- Actually, I have an appointment...

267
00:14:48,768 --> 00:14:51,660
I'm getting ready to open my business,
so I don't have business cards yet.

268
00:14:51,660 --> 00:14:54,328
Oh, I happen to have a business card.

269
00:14:54,328 --> 00:14:55,396
- Oh, yes, if you give it to me...
- Please contact me.

270
00:14:55,396 --> 00:14:56,984
- Yeah, may I?
- Yeah.

271
00:14:56,984 --> 00:14:58,920
- I'm Joo Bo Sung.
- Oh, yes.

272
00:14:58,920 --> 00:15:00,516
Yeah.

273
00:15:08,444 --> 00:15:10,408
Were you on drugs?

274
00:15:10,408 --> 00:15:11,842
What?

275
00:15:11,842 --> 00:15:13,960
Or is this about a woman? What is it?

276
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:17,580
You're not the type to get accused
of sexual harassment, are you?

277
00:15:19,140 --> 00:15:23,516
Or did you get scammed?
Did you scam someone? Which is it?

278
00:15:24,316 --> 00:15:27,316
- Careful, careful.
- Wait, my foot...

279
00:15:27,316 --> 00:15:29,292
Hang on, my hips!

280
00:15:29,292 --> 00:15:31,636
Come on, what's with you?

281
00:15:31,636 --> 00:15:35,184
Is that really the only image you have of me?

282
00:15:35,184 --> 00:15:37,740
Then why do you suddenly
need that much money?

283
00:15:37,740 --> 00:15:41,149
Not even 100 million won,
109 million won? What's that?

284
00:15:42,555 --> 00:15:46,749
Well, things got a bit complicated.

285
00:15:48,683 --> 00:15:50,328
All right, I'll lend it to you.

286
00:15:50,328 --> 00:15:53,040
I'm only lending it to you because it's you.

287
00:15:53,040 --> 00:15:55,876
Really? Are you sure?

288
00:15:55,876 --> 00:15:58,078
Min Woo, thank you so much.

289
00:15:58,078 --> 00:15:59,352
Wow, that's amazing!

290
00:15:59,352 --> 00:16:00,816
That's enough.

291
00:16:04,008 --> 00:16:06,040
I can't cover all of it,

292
00:16:06,040 --> 00:16:09,824
but I'll chip in what I can, okay?

293
00:16:09,824 --> 00:16:10,900
Yeah, well...

294
00:16:10,900 --> 00:16:14,668
That's more than enough.
Times are tough these days.

295
00:16:14,668 --> 00:16:18,388
But... how much...

296
00:16:18,388 --> 00:16:20,008
[Kim Min Woo transferred 10,000,000 won]

297
00:16:20,008 --> 00:16:22,552
Jeez, you've got to be kidding me.

298
00:16:22,552 --> 00:16:24,783
What, 10 million won...

299
00:16:27,936 --> 00:16:29,364
He keeps bragging about
making money off crypto

300
00:16:29,364 --> 00:16:32,016
while blowing it all at hostess bars.

301
00:16:37,549 --> 00:16:40,883
[Contacts]

302
00:16:40,883 --> 00:16:42,764
[Min Seo's Mother]

303
00:16:46,508 --> 00:16:50,361
And Chairwoman, how about checking
the financial statements one more time?

304
00:16:50,361 --> 00:16:53,549
It's been a while,
and it'd be safer that way.

305
00:16:59,542 --> 00:17:01,783
Have you been waiting long?

306
00:17:01,783 --> 00:17:04,583
Now, it's time to sign.

307
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:09,916
One last step.

308
00:17:09,916 --> 00:17:12,983
We just need to complete one more
financial due diligence review.

309
00:17:14,248 --> 00:17:16,383
Oh, financial due diligence...

310
00:17:17,936 --> 00:17:19,883
Another financial due diligence review?

311
00:17:20,592 --> 00:17:25,552
Was there something lacking
when you did it before?

312
00:17:25,552 --> 00:17:28,288
Some time has passed since then.

313
00:17:28,288 --> 00:17:30,560
Just a formality.

314
00:17:30,560 --> 00:17:36,116
You know how some startup CEOs
treat company money like it's their own.

315
00:17:36,116 --> 00:17:39,664
I'm sure you're not like that, though.

316
00:17:39,664 --> 00:17:41,388
Right?

317
00:17:41,388 --> 00:17:44,116
Oh, of course not.

318
00:17:47,768 --> 00:17:49,028
Yeah, I got it.

319
00:17:49,028 --> 00:17:50,357
If anything happens to Min Seo,

320
00:17:50,357 --> 00:17:55,024
no, if anything happens to Ye Ji too,
call me right away.

321
00:17:55,024 --> 00:17:56,516
Yeah.

322
00:17:57,572 --> 00:17:59,500
[Authorized Personnel Only]
Even if it's something small, it's okay.

323
00:17:59,500 --> 00:18:01,660
You know what I mean, right?

324
00:18:01,660 --> 00:18:03,116
Yeah.

325
00:18:06,916 --> 00:18:08,672
You could've come to the hospital.

326
00:18:08,672 --> 00:18:10,716
Oh, that's...

327
00:18:11,611 --> 00:18:15,892
Wow! This trash can is still here.

328
00:18:15,892 --> 00:18:19,600
Remember when there was a fire here,
and you put it out with a fire extinguisher?

329
00:18:19,600 --> 00:18:22,144
That's when I totally fell for you.

330
00:18:22,144 --> 00:18:26,249
Oh... Yeah, that's right.

331
00:18:29,692 --> 00:18:31,692
You've been going through a lot lately

332
00:18:31,692 --> 00:18:34,852
with the divorce and the custody battle.

333
00:18:34,852 --> 00:18:38,312
Is there anything I can do to help?

334
00:18:38,312 --> 00:18:42,616
I'd do anything for you, anything.

335
00:18:42,616 --> 00:18:44,352
You know how I feel, right?

336
00:18:44,352 --> 00:18:45,568
I do.

337
00:18:45,568 --> 00:18:48,972
You know I trust and rely on you too,
Jae Hong, right?

338
00:18:48,972 --> 00:18:50,383
Of course.

339
00:18:53,716 --> 00:18:56,116
Is that why you wanted to see me?

340
00:19:02,748 --> 00:19:06,083
I'm really not the kind of person
who does this.

341
00:19:08,100 --> 00:19:12,676
I really didn't want to say this to you...

342
00:19:12,676 --> 00:19:16,583
Why? Is something wrong?

343
00:19:18,336 --> 00:19:19,783
I'm...

344
00:19:21,357 --> 00:19:24,683
I'm so sorry,

345
00:19:26,220 --> 00:19:28,849
but can you lend me 99 million won?

346
00:19:34,216 --> 00:19:38,195
Right, I know. It's so sudden.

347
00:19:38,195 --> 00:19:40,883
I know, I know,

348
00:19:40,883 --> 00:19:45,324
but I'm desperate
if I'm asking you for money...

349
00:19:45,324 --> 00:19:47,052
No, that's not it.

350
00:19:47,052 --> 00:19:49,140
Honey,

351
00:19:49,140 --> 00:19:52,949
I'm asking you this because I trust you.

352
00:19:54,960 --> 00:19:58,336
I feel like I'm dying of stress now.

353
00:19:58,336 --> 00:20:01,176
I mean, I don't have any way to come up
with that much money.

354
00:20:01,176 --> 00:20:04,636
How am I supposed to come up
with 500 million won in a single day...

355
00:20:04,636 --> 00:20:06,149
A single day?

356
00:20:06,988 --> 00:20:10,312
Did something happen yesterday?

357
00:20:10,312 --> 00:20:12,984
Are you in trouble?

358
00:20:12,984 --> 00:20:15,116
That villa...

359
00:20:15,116 --> 00:20:17,849
Well, they said the balance for the villa
has to be paid by today.

360
00:20:17,849 --> 00:20:21,236
They said it'd be a disaster if I don't pay.

361
00:20:21,236 --> 00:20:23,049
Even so...

362
00:20:24,044 --> 00:20:28,683
I guess it's too much to ask, right?

363
00:20:29,836 --> 00:20:33,449
Right, no matter how much we love each other,

364
00:20:33,449 --> 00:20:37,876
99 million won on such short notice

365
00:20:37,876 --> 00:20:41,583
is a lot, right?

366
00:20:43,896 --> 00:20:47,444
But I'm going to be the lead
in a drama this time.

367
00:20:47,444 --> 00:20:51,649
So I should be able to pay you back
in just a few months.

368
00:20:52,772 --> 00:20:54,972
Soo Jung.

369
00:20:54,972 --> 00:20:57,304
Soo Jung, you trust me, don't you?

370
00:20:57,304 --> 00:20:59,172
Right?

371
00:20:59,172 --> 00:21:03,188
If you get that money,
everything will be okay?

372
00:21:03,188 --> 00:21:05,916
It'll solve everything for sure?

373
00:21:05,916 --> 00:21:08,349
Yeah, it will.

374
00:21:10,602 --> 00:21:13,160
Okay. I'll lend it to you.

375
00:21:13,160 --> 00:21:18,352
I can't just stand by
while you're struggling, Jae Hong.

376
00:21:18,352 --> 00:21:19,849
Really?

377
00:21:20,836 --> 00:21:24,208
Oh, god...

378
00:21:24,208 --> 00:21:28,883
You're the only one I can count on, really.

379
00:21:35,016 --> 00:21:36,588
I love you.

380
00:21:36,588 --> 00:21:38,700
I really do.

381
00:21:38,700 --> 00:21:40,404
Thank you so much, honey.

382
00:21:40,404 --> 00:21:45,183
I don't know how
I'll ever repay you for this.

383
00:21:46,040 --> 00:21:49,404
I'll text you the account number now.

384
00:21:49,404 --> 00:21:51,283
This, yeah...

385
00:21:53,080 --> 00:21:55,674
But it's really urgent.

386
00:21:55,674 --> 00:21:57,017
Alright.

387
00:21:57,017 --> 00:21:59,249
- I'll transfer it right away.
- Yeah, okay.

388
00:22:00,176 --> 00:22:01,916
Boo Jin still isn't answering?

389
00:22:01,916 --> 00:22:03,784
No, she hasn't even read my texts.

390
00:22:03,784 --> 00:22:06,144
I'm swamped, seriously.

391
00:22:06,144 --> 00:22:07,816
I wonder what's going on.

392
00:22:20,676 --> 00:22:22,083
<i>Yeah, honey.</i>

393
00:22:23,276 --> 00:22:26,428
Guess who managed to borrow
100 million won in just 30 minutes.

394
00:22:26,428 --> 00:22:27,716
<i>Who could it be, who could it be?</i>

395
00:22:27,716 --> 00:22:30,572
- Your husband Lim Jae Hong, huh?
- <i>Wow.</i>

396
00:22:30,572 --> 00:22:34,108
<i>That's really amazing. You did great, honey.</i>

397
00:22:34,108 --> 00:22:35,420
I know.

398
00:22:35,420 --> 00:22:38,700
<i>But who lent you that much money?</i>

399
00:22:38,700 --> 00:22:41,000
The CEO, yeah.

400
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:44,316
- I finally landed that lead role.
- <i>Yeah, that's right, that's right.</i>

401
00:22:44,316 --> 00:22:46,872
- Honey, the elevator's here.
- <i>Okay.</i>

402
00:22:46,872 --> 00:22:50,049
- Everything's settled, so I'm heading home.
- <i>Alright.</i>

403
00:23:12,244 --> 00:23:14,592
Sir, I'm sorry, but I'll get off here.

404
00:23:14,592 --> 00:23:15,883
Here?

405
00:23:15,883 --> 00:23:18,549
- Yeah, alright.
- Thank you.

406
00:23:24,952 --> 00:23:27,383
Sir, I'll get off too!

407
00:23:36,916 --> 00:23:38,816
[Bonggak-dong District 2 transforms,
SJ Construction will be with you!]

408
00:23:46,563 --> 00:23:48,643
<i>The subscriber you have dialed
is not available.</i>

409
00:23:48,643 --> 00:23:50,438
<i>You'll be connected to the voice mail.</i>

410
00:23:50,438 --> 00:23:53,004
Why isn't this punk answering the phone?

411
00:23:53,004 --> 00:23:54,792
Huh?

412
00:23:54,792 --> 00:23:56,449
What?

413
00:25:04,383 --> 00:25:08,583
[Mom]

414
00:25:10,644 --> 00:25:13,032
<i>Min Seo, are you at the academy?</i>

415
00:25:13,032 --> 00:25:16,672
- Yeah.
- <i>It's nothing, but did Ye Ji</i>

416
00:25:16,672 --> 00:25:18,749
- What are you doing there?
- <i>talk to her dad or something?</i>

417
00:25:18,749 --> 00:25:21,616
<i>Did she say anything unusual?</i>

418
00:25:23,228 --> 00:25:24,560
- Excuse me?
- <i>Min Seo, Min Seo?</i>

419
00:25:24,560 --> 00:25:27,549
- Pardon?
- What were you doing here?

420
00:25:31,208 --> 00:25:33,483
- Well...
- Min Seo!

421
00:25:35,788 --> 00:25:38,483
The cats all ran that way!

422
00:25:40,187 --> 00:25:41,720
They all went over there.

423
00:25:41,720 --> 00:25:43,438
I checked here earlier.
There isn't a single one.

424
00:25:43,438 --> 00:25:45,049
We need to go that way.

425
00:25:52,848 --> 00:25:54,549
Just look straight ahead and go.

426
00:26:12,312 --> 00:26:14,564
About yesterday...

427
00:26:14,564 --> 00:26:16,149
I was too hard on you...

428
00:26:16,149 --> 00:26:18,083
But that guy.

429
00:26:19,200 --> 00:26:22,256
Doesn't he kind of look
like the man from yesterday?

430
00:26:22,256 --> 00:26:23,716
Huh?

431
00:26:24,900 --> 00:26:26,483
That guy?

432
00:26:27,660 --> 00:26:29,249
Did you see his face?

433
00:26:31,052 --> 00:26:35,136
No, not really...

434
00:26:35,136 --> 00:26:36,583
It couldn't be.

435
00:26:36,583 --> 00:26:40,812
[40 Minutes Until the Video Release]

436
00:26:49,268 --> 00:26:50,964
What's with the designer bag?

437
00:26:50,964 --> 00:26:53,540
Is it a free gift for that punk?

438
00:26:53,540 --> 00:26:56,123
Oh, so we're handing over the bag too.

439
00:26:56,123 --> 00:26:59,108
Check the storage room.
There's a duffel bag that you used to use.

440
00:26:59,108 --> 00:27:00,916
Oh, okay.

441
00:27:14,016 --> 00:27:18,016
[Self Defense Pepper Spray]

442
00:28:32,149 --> 00:28:35,016
[2 Minutes Until the Video Release]

443
00:28:37,868 --> 00:28:39,849
I'll run ahead first.

444
00:28:49,983 --> 00:28:52,108
[Breaking! The shocking secret
of a perfect family]

445
00:29:32,283 --> 00:29:35,683
[Release Imminent, 00:00:11]

446
00:29:51,516 --> 00:29:53,816
[Error]

447
00:29:59,908 --> 00:30:01,649
Yeah, you saw that link, right?

448
00:30:01,649 --> 00:30:03,000
<i>Yeah, I saw it.</i>

449
00:30:03,000 --> 00:30:06,249
Jeez, that's taken care of for now.

450
00:30:08,407 --> 00:30:12,940
Honey, I'll wait
inside the drugstore next door,

451
00:30:12,940 --> 00:30:14,316
and when they come to pick up the money...

452
00:30:14,316 --> 00:30:15,780
<i>Yeah, good job.</i>

453
00:30:15,780 --> 00:30:18,045
<i>- Just come out through the east entrance.</i>
- Huh?

454
00:30:18,045 --> 00:30:19,883
Now it begins.

455
00:30:21,318 --> 00:30:22,597
Let go, let go.

456
00:30:22,597 --> 00:30:25,312
I said I'd show you!

457
00:30:25,312 --> 00:30:27,783
- Seriously, let go!
- I said I want to see.

458
00:30:29,604 --> 00:30:32,783
Wait, what are you planning to do?

459
00:30:32,783 --> 00:30:35,796
[GPS Tracks Live]

460
00:30:35,796 --> 00:30:38,169
Huh? What's this?

461
00:30:38,169 --> 00:30:40,704
A GPS tracker?

462
00:30:40,704 --> 00:30:43,764
Wow. That's genius.

463
00:30:43,764 --> 00:30:45,683
When did you set this up, honey?

464
00:30:47,624 --> 00:30:50,416
Wow, as expected of my wife.

465
00:30:52,000 --> 00:30:53,261
That's amazing, really!

466
00:30:53,261 --> 00:30:54,948
Wow, I've only ever seen
stuff like this in movies.

467
00:30:54,948 --> 00:30:57,132
I never would've thought of this.

468
00:30:57,132 --> 00:30:58,483
What's this?

469
00:30:59,296 --> 00:31:01,249
Looks like they got on the subway.

470
00:31:57,696 --> 00:31:59,249
- Is that the punk?
- Is it him?

471
00:32:03,933 --> 00:32:06,328
- What's going on?
- What?

472
00:32:06,328 --> 00:32:08,716
Huh? Not here. This way, this way.

473
00:32:08,716 --> 00:32:10,349
Yeah.

474
00:32:13,516 --> 00:32:15,280
There, that.

475
00:32:15,280 --> 00:32:16,816
There...

476
00:32:40,144 --> 00:32:41,580
Let's go inside.

477
00:32:41,580 --> 00:32:43,049
Yeah, okay.

478
00:32:43,888 --> 00:32:45,349
Let's go in.

479
00:32:49,428 --> 00:32:52,552
Shouldn't I handle the negotiation?

480
00:32:52,552 --> 00:32:55,304
If it takes too long

481
00:32:55,304 --> 00:32:59,340
or someone else shows up,
then you come up right away.

482
00:32:59,340 --> 00:33:01,849
Yeah, good idea.

483
00:33:03,080 --> 00:33:04,812
Honey, good luck and come back.

484
00:33:04,812 --> 00:33:07,683
Yeah, fighting.

485
00:33:15,683 --> 00:33:17,143
[Jae Hong, it's been bothering me]

486
00:33:17,143 --> 00:33:19,349
[Is that thing
you mentioned yesterday serious?]

487
00:33:19,349 --> 00:33:23,583
[Did everything work out?
You can tell me anything]

488
00:33:40,708 --> 00:33:42,096
Joo Min Seo!

489
00:33:42,096 --> 00:33:46,500
Why didn't you answer your phone?

490
00:33:46,500 --> 00:33:48,640
Mom...

491
00:33:48,640 --> 00:33:51,484
There were tire tracks there,

492
00:33:51,484 --> 00:33:54,055
and some man there...

493
00:33:54,055 --> 00:33:56,704
What are you talking about?
Don't tell me you went back there.

494
00:33:56,704 --> 00:33:58,283
Joo Min Seo! You...

495
00:34:00,315 --> 00:34:02,390
Say it again properly, okay?

496
00:34:02,390 --> 00:34:05,800
Who was that man? What did he do?

497
00:34:05,800 --> 00:34:08,536
I don't know who he was,

498
00:34:08,536 --> 00:34:11,876
but he kept asking what I'd been doing there

499
00:34:11,876 --> 00:34:14,596
and was looking at the tire tracks...

500
00:34:14,596 --> 00:34:16,472
- I didn't tell him anything...
- The tire tracks are still there?

501
00:34:16,472 --> 00:34:18,648
Wait, who is that man?

502
00:34:18,648 --> 00:34:21,244
I should've checked more carefully yesterday.

503
00:34:21,244 --> 00:34:23,083
Oh, seriously...

504
00:34:24,148 --> 00:34:27,583
I shouldn't have just left it
to the neighbors.

505
00:34:29,216 --> 00:34:32,684
[Min Seo's Mother]

506
00:34:58,272 --> 00:34:59,849
Delivery!

507
00:35:05,068 --> 00:35:07,083
Please confirm your package!

508
00:35:26,668 --> 00:35:28,283
Huh?

509
00:35:33,012 --> 00:35:34,949
- Captain Park?
- Crystal Dermatology?

510
00:35:37,684 --> 00:35:39,164
No, no, no.

511
00:35:39,164 --> 00:35:41,316
No, no, no, no.

512
00:35:41,316 --> 00:35:45,020
I'm not here to fight. Just calm down.

513
00:35:45,020 --> 00:35:47,683
I just want to make sure
you delete the original video.

514
00:35:50,316 --> 00:35:53,144
You came all the way here
just to verify that?

515
00:35:53,144 --> 00:35:54,952
Of course, I did.

516
00:35:54,952 --> 00:35:57,516
I paid you 500 million won!

517
00:36:03,188 --> 00:36:04,188
Oh, I'll...

518
00:36:05,012 --> 00:36:07,368
I'll delete it.

519
00:36:07,368 --> 00:36:09,556
Come in.

520
00:36:09,556 --> 00:36:11,983
You'll delete it? Wait...

521
00:36:13,076 --> 00:36:14,716
Thank you.

522
00:36:26,440 --> 00:36:29,176
I'll delete the original.

523
00:36:29,176 --> 00:36:32,549
This is the backup copy.

524
00:36:36,805 --> 00:36:38,283
By the way,

525
00:36:39,208 --> 00:36:41,116
I'm a huge fan.

526
00:36:42,488 --> 00:36:44,049
Seriously.

527
00:36:49,932 --> 00:36:52,738
I've bought all the merch.

528
00:36:52,738 --> 00:36:54,916
In the summer,
I use that umbrella all the time.

529
00:36:54,916 --> 00:36:57,883
See this pouch?

530
00:36:57,883 --> 00:36:59,464
And... oh!

531
00:36:59,464 --> 00:37:01,726
And this new item
in your online shop is so cute...

532
00:37:01,726 --> 00:37:06,183
Oh. You're looking at that now?

533
00:37:06,816 --> 00:37:07,916
[Allow USB debugging, 100%]

534
00:37:07,916 --> 00:37:09,549
[backups]

535
00:37:21,732 --> 00:37:23,483
Good.

536
00:37:47,400 --> 00:37:50,435
Why on earth
are you living with such a loser?

537
00:37:50,435 --> 00:37:53,183
Just divorce him already.

538
00:37:55,276 --> 00:37:59,348
Captain Park, why would you come
all the way here yourself?

539
00:37:59,348 --> 00:38:01,368
Well, I'm glad you did,

540
00:38:01,368 --> 00:38:03,036
but honestly, Lim Jae Hong
should've been the one to come.

541
00:38:03,036 --> 00:38:05,316
Oh, how frustrating.

542
00:38:07,244 --> 00:38:11,584
And honestly, you earned all this money.

543
00:38:11,584 --> 00:38:14,249
Well... I did take a little of it.

544
00:38:15,900 --> 00:38:18,520
So divorce him.

545
00:38:18,520 --> 00:38:22,628
As a true crew member,
I'm really begging you.

546
00:38:22,628 --> 00:38:24,284
Have a safe divorce.

547
00:38:24,284 --> 00:38:25,883
Okay?

548
00:39:18,312 --> 00:39:21,960
Huh? Honey, are you okay?

549
00:39:21,960 --> 00:39:26,496
You were taking so long
I was about to come up!

550
00:39:26,496 --> 00:39:28,456
What happened?

551
00:39:28,456 --> 00:39:31,540
What, did you just give her the money?

552
00:39:31,540 --> 00:39:33,012
Did you see the video?

553
00:39:33,012 --> 00:39:35,575
What, was Ye Ji's face all caught on it?

554
00:39:35,575 --> 00:39:40,020
Don't tell me we were both on it!

555
00:39:40,020 --> 00:39:41,896
What happened?

556
00:39:41,896 --> 00:39:43,748
Honey.

557
00:39:43,748 --> 00:39:45,216
Wait...

558
00:39:46,516 --> 00:39:48,016
What...

559
00:40:29,237 --> 00:40:32,173
Anyway, it worked out, right?

560
00:40:32,173 --> 00:40:33,649
Right?

561
00:40:37,316 --> 00:40:39,884
[Min Seo's Mother]

562
00:40:46,660 --> 00:40:49,372
Anyway, you did well.

563
00:40:49,372 --> 00:40:54,183
Let's just call it bad luck
and move on, okay?

564
00:40:58,383 --> 00:41:00,236
[Min Seo's Mother]

565
00:41:04,273 --> 00:41:06,549
From now on, as you said, honey,

566
00:41:07,332 --> 00:41:11,349
let's really live well, okay?

567
00:42:54,860 --> 00:42:57,879
You punk, serves you right!
You piece of crap...

568
00:42:57,879 --> 00:43:00,883
You piece of crap, you punk!

569
00:43:15,153 --> 00:43:18,083
Hey, you trash!

570
00:43:31,212 --> 00:43:33,216
You piece of crap.

571
00:43:33,216 --> 00:43:35,016
You piece of crap!

572
00:43:35,016 --> 00:43:36,049
Die!

573
00:43:36,049 --> 00:43:39,316
- You piece of crap.
- Let go, you punk!

574
00:44:13,749 --> 00:44:15,449
Shoot!

575
00:44:19,752 --> 00:44:21,249
Darn it.

576
00:44:22,923 --> 00:44:24,683
Darn it!

577
00:44:25,949 --> 00:44:29,416
[Accident Occurred, March 30, 9:04 PM]

578
00:44:29,416 --> 00:44:35,116
[Incident Occurred, March 30, 9:23 PM]

